cartridge "PIRATE COVE/Barbara H. Schulak/1986"

' PIRATE COVE
' A ColecoVision game based on "Pirate Cove", a mini-adventure for kids
' by Barbara H. Schulak, COMPUTE!'s Gazette, August 1986 (Commodore 64,
' BASIC; the listing names no author: the name is from the LaunchBox
' games database). Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by
' Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game (orig/pirate_cove.bas): a 5 x 5 sea of 25 places. Ten are land
' (TREASURE ISLAND, SEA MONSTER'S LAIR, PIRATE COVE and seven more), 15
' are HIGH SEAS, shuffled anew each game (lines 340-380). You start at
' PIRATE COVE. Each land place but the treasure and the monster has two
' things to search, given out in map order (lines 390-480): one search
' finds A KEY, one A CUTLASS, others treasures or nothing. Menus: search,
' READ MAP (land and water, not which island is which), SAIL ON
' (NORTH/SOUTH/EAST/WEST; off the edge: STORM AHEAD-GO ANOTHER WAY),
' LIST INVENTORY. At the SEA MONSTER'S LAIR: SAIL AWAY (one chance in
' five to get away, else the ship is damaged and you go back to PIRATE
' COVE) or FIGHT (a cutlass wins; without one, back to PIRATE COVE).
' TREASURE ISLAND: with the key the chest opens, YOU WIN and your other
' treasures are listed; without it, sail on and find the key.
'
' Kept from the listing: the 25 places and their shuffle, the place
' names, the 16 searches and their finds in the listing's order and the
' way they are given out, the inventory rule (finds starting NOTHING are
' not kept, no doubles), the movement table (edges are storms), the
' monster's odds and outcomes, the treasure chest, every message (lines
' longer than 28 columns are wrapped).
'
' Liberties:
' - The listing's menus moved a bar with the cursor-down key and RETURN;
'   here the stick moves a pointer up and down (it wraps) and either side
'   button chooses. "PRESS ANY KEY" is a button.
' - Two places are named after this port's own made-up captains:
'   BLUEBEARD'S BAY is REDSAIL BAY and CAPT. HOOK'S SWAMP is CAPT. MAREN'S
'   SWAMP (no pirates from books or films); SEARCH NATIVE HUTS is SEARCH
'   FISHING HUTS.
' - The map marks islands you have visited with a flag (the listing only
'   showed land, water and where you are), so a young player need not
'   remember them. Places are still unnamed on the map.
' - The pictures are new: each place shows sky and sea with the ship;
'   land has an island with a palm, the treasure island a chest, the lair
'   the sea monster, a storm grey clouds. New sounds and an original
'   title tune ("Lanterns on the Cove"). The win waits for the button
'   and goes back to the title (no PLAY AGAIN question).
' - The winner's screen lists the treasures under OTHER TREASURES as the
'   listing did; the slow border flash is left out.
'
' Controls: either controller; stick up/down and a side button (no keypad).
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128;
' screens drawn with the NMI and the display off; the title tune once,
' music first in the sound table.

